      "writtenOn": "2024-01-02T18:49:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can we just call it `paintColor`? The shared aspect feels like a cool optimization/implementation detail, but when we\u0027re reading shader code it will be much clearer to see `half4 c \u003d paintColor;` instead of `half4 c \u003d paintColorSingleton;`.\n\nIf anything, the method name might be a better place for this--`Uniform::PaintColorSingleton()` or `Uniform::SharedPaintColor()` perhaps? (I\u0027m thinking this is not quite the \"singleton\" pattern since each set of uniforms will have its own paint color. \"Singleton\" typically means _exactly_ one instance of a class: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singleton_pattern)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 37,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 37,
        "endChar": 43
      },
      "revId": "e021b58e8f903b73184cf702634e015c126799e4",
